  "notes/AGENTS.md": "<!-- agent-notes:begin -->\n## Engineering decision Notes\n\nBefore planning related changes or first editing code, run `node .agents/notes/runtime/cli.mjs context --paths <project-relative-paths> --topic <topic>` from the project root. Include new, deleted and renamed paths; query again when scope or approach changes. Read only relevant returned Notes with `show <id>` or their paths.\n\nUse `agent-note` when durable rationale or discarded alternatives cannot live in code, tests or existing docs: suggest recording, then proceed on user acceptance or an explicit request; retain existing authorization. Ordinary Plan may finish with zero Notes. Ship required Notes with code in the same PR. Use `agent-note-maintenance` for lifecycle changes and cleanup; run `check` before delivery. [Command inputs and lifecycle rules](.agents/notes/runtime/assets/references/writing.md) are available when writing or maintaining a Note.\n<!-- agent-notes:end -->\n",
